  released file's symbols): AnvilMac Scripts/runtime/native-fullscreen-check.sh: a resizable 800 x 600 test window
  becomes 1728 x 1084 about 1.1 s after its last frame change (64- and 32-bit, also after an early resize) and stays so
  when it resizes itself to 1280 x 800 in full screen; unchanged without the variable, on the control, for fixed-size
  and small windows. Owner, Warcraft III: fullscreen, edge scrolling, menu bar hidden (2026-11-01/02); the arrow after
  clicks went away on the next move with the activation reassert. Owner, candidate 9: edges fine (confinement traced 1728 x 1084 throughout). Candidate 10: edges and Dock fine (presentation options
  0x40a after every activation); right-click arrow remained. Refusal while entering: owner session pending (an untraced candidate-11 session
  had bottom/right edges unreachable again). Full-screen decisions (entering, client frame requests, confinements, presentation options)
  are traced on their own channel, nativefs, which AnvilMac turns on with the variable, as are
  the cursor changes Wine makes in such a session (for the remaining right-click arrow).

